From: Balena RK3588 integration
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip_sdhci: pulse the device-tree reset lines at probe

The kernel's rk35xx_sdhci_reset() (drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-dwcmshc.c)
asserts and deasserts every reset control named in the device tree
(resets/reset-names: core, bus, axi, block, timer) whenever it performs
SDHCI_RESET_ALL.  On boards whose earlier boot stages leave the eMMC host
controller wedged, that pulse is what recovers the host: Linux enumerates
the card while this vendor U-Boot driver, which never touches the resets,
fails every mmc 0 init with "Card did not respond to voltage select"
(-95) in both SPL and U-Boot proper.

Mirror the kernel sequence, not just the pulse:

- assert every declared reset line, hold 1 us, then release them all
  (the kernel holds a reset_control_array, so the lines move as a group
  instead of being pulsed one at a time);
- run the SDHCI software reset afterwards -- that is what clears the
  command/data state machines and their PRESENT_STATE inhibit bits;
- re-enable the vendor internal clock gate (DWCMSHC_EMMC_MISC_CON bit 1)
  which the CRU pulse wipes.

Without the two post-pulse steps the first rockchip_emmc_set_clock()
after probe stalls with "Timeout to wait cmd & data inhibit" and every
command escalates into a busy timeout, which is what the 11:52 batch
showed on the board.  The DM reset API is already enabled for both
U-Boot proper and SPL in the board defconfig, so the same code path
covers both stages.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/rockchip_sdhci.c b/bsp/rockchip-sdk/source/u-boot/drivers/mmc/rockchip_sdhci.c
index 373b634a9..9c36ce6d4 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/rockchip_sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/rockchip_sdhci.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <malloc.h>
 #include <mapmem.h>
 #include <sdhci.h>
+#include <reset.h>
 #include <clk.h>
 #include <syscon.h>
 #include <dm/ofnode.h>
@@ -59,6 +60,9 @@ DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
 #define DWCMSHC_EMMC_DLL_TXCLK		0x808
 #define DWCMSHC_EMMC_DLL_STRBIN		0x80c
 #define DECMSHC_EMMC_DLL_CMDOUT		0x810
+/* Same register the kernel driver calls DECMSHC_EMMC_MISC_CON. */
+#define DWCMSHC_EMMC_MISC_CON		0x81c
+#define DWCMSHC_MISC_INTCLK_EN		BIT(1)
 #define DWCMSHC_EMMC_DLL_STATUS0	0x840
 #define DWCMSHC_EMMC_DLL_STATUS1	0x844
 #define DWCMSHC_EMMC_DLL_START		BIT(0)
@@ -557,6 +561,57 @@ static int rockchip_sdhci_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 		printf("%s fail to get clk\n", __func__);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The kernel's rk35xx_sdhci_reset() pulses all device-tree reset
+	 * controls (core/bus/axi/block/timer) on SDHCI_RESET_ALL; a host
+	 * left wedged by earlier boot stages only recovers after that
+	 * pulse.  This driver never touched the resets, so mmc 0 init
+	 * failed with "Card did not respond to voltage select" (-95) even
+	 * though the same chip enumerates fine under Linux.  Mirror the
+	 * kernel sequence exactly: the reset lines are asserted and
+	 * released as a group (the kernel holds a reset_control_array),
+	 * then the SDHCI software reset clears the command/data state
+	 * machines (the inhibit bits), and finally the vendor internal
+	 * clock gate wiped by the CRU pulse is re-enabled.  Without those
+	 * two post-pulse steps the first rockchip_emmc_set_clock() stalls
+	 * with "Timeout to wait cmd & data inhibit" and every command
+	 * ends in a busy timeout.
+	 */
+	{
+		struct reset_ctl rst;
+		u32 extra = sdhci_readl(host, DWCMSHC_EMMC_MISC_CON);
+		unsigned long timeout;
+		int i, count;
+
+		for (i = 0;; i++) {
+			ret = reset_get_by_index(dev, i, &rst);
+			if (ret)
+				break;
+			reset_assert(&rst);
+		}
+		count = i;
+		udelay(1);
+		for (i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+			reset_get_by_index(dev, i, &rst);
+			reset_deassert(&rst);
+		}
+
+		sdhci_writeb(host, SDHCI_RESET_ALL, SDHCI_SOFTWARE_RESET);
+		timeout = 100;
+		while (sdhci_readb(host, SDHCI_SOFTWARE_RESET) & SDHCI_RESET_ALL) {
+			if (timeout == 0) {
+				printf("%s: Reset 0x%x never completed.\n",
+				       __func__, (int)SDHCI_RESET_ALL);
+				break;
+			}
+			timeout--;
+			udelay(1000);
+		}
+
+		sdhci_writel(host, DWCMSHC_MISC_INTCLK_EN | extra,
+			     DWCMSHC_EMMC_MISC_CON);
+	}
+
 	prv->emmc_clk = clk;
 	prv->dev = dev;
 	ret = data->get_phy(dev);
